---
title: V60 Hot
coffee:
  id: v60-hot
  brewer: v60
  brewerName: V60
  label: Hot
  legacyVariant: hot
  size: "02"
  min: 12
  max: 30
  dose: 20
  grind: Encore · 15
  texture: Start medium-fine, a little finer than table salt. Original Encore, not ESP. Adjust to taste; calibration varies.
  temperature: 201–205°F
  temperatureF: 203
  order: 10
  icon: "▽"
  description: A clean, bright cup
---

= Prep =
Rinse the filter, warm the brewer, then discard the rinse water. Add @coffee{20%g} to the #V60{} and make a small well in the center.

= Bloom =
Wet all the grounds with @water{60%g} over ~{15%seconds}, then give the brewer a gentle swirl.

= Let it bloom =
Let the coffee release its gas. No water needed. Wait until ~until{45%seconds} on the brew clock.

= Pour 1 =
Pour @water{86 2/3%g} over ~{25%seconds} in slow circles, from the center outward. Avoid the filter walls.

= Let it settle =
Give the water time to drain through the bed for ~{20%seconds}.

= Pour 2 =
Pour @water{86 2/3%g} over ~{25%seconds} in slow circles, from the center outward. Avoid the filter walls.

= Let it settle =
Give the water time to drain through the bed for ~{20%seconds}.

= Pour 3 =
Pour @water{86 2/3%g} over ~{25%seconds} in slow circles, from the center outward. Avoid the filter walls.

= Draw down =
Gently swirl to level the bed. Let the remaining water drain until ~until{210%seconds} on the brew clock.

= Finish =
Swirl, sip, and tell your journal how it went.
